      "slug": "300-club",
      "question": "What is the 300 Club?",
      "answer": "It is the elite tier, for a child who out-scores 99 percent of high-school seniors on any proctored MAP subject. The thresholds are 281 in Math, 261 in Reading, 259 in Language and 247 in Science. A 300 in Math is a perfect score, the ceiling of the whole scale — in all of Austin perhaps one child reaches it, perhaps nobody does.\n\nReaching it moves a student out of the children's contest and into the SAT level. Members get an official SAT sitting paid for by gt.school, auto-qualify for the in-person finals, and walk out with a scholarship offer.\n\nThere is prize money on the SAT ladder too: $1,000 at 1300, $5,000 at 1400, $10,000 at 1500, and $25,000 at 1575.",
