      "answer": "You do. A child cannot register themselves. The program is built around the parent account: a parent registers first, and the child's account only follows after the parent completes verifiable parental consent.\n\nNo personal information is collected from a child online before that consent is given. A parent or guardian also signs the entry, any publicity release, and prize acceptance.\n\nThe specific steps that verifiable parental consent involves have not been published yet; the program says they will be part of the sign-up flow when registration opens on August 3.",
