      "slug": "top-prizes",
      "question": "What are the top prizes?",
      "answer": "Two $100,000 subject crowns sit at the top: the Math/Science Crown for the best young mathematician and the Reading/Language Crown for the best young reader, each awarded for the highest proctored segment score in the metro. There is no overall composite prize, but the crowns stack — one child topping both boards wins the $200,000 Double Crown.\n\nThe $50,000 Effort Grand is the third pillar. It goes to the most Timeback XP, which counts only for mastered work at each child's own level, so any child can win it regardless of how far ahead they already are.\n\nBelow those sit $10,000 grade champions, $5,000 grade effort champions, and guaranteed $1,000 champions in every one of the 92 eligible ZIP codes. Verified Grade Level completions also earn $1,000 bounties, limited to the first 250 and a maximum of three per student. In total the program puts the prize pool at over $350,000.\n\nTwo things are not published yet: the tie-break rule if two children finish level on a crown, and an official rules document.",
